# Trivy accepted findings — each is justified below. Real, fixable findings are
# NOT listed here (the OTel/grpc CVEs were fixed by dependency bumps, and the
# operator deployment was hardened with a full securityContext). What remains are
# findings that are either inherent to a Kubernetes operator's function or are
# handled by Kubernetes-native controls rather than the image/manifest itself.
# Multiple ID forms per finding are listed so the match works regardless of the
# Trivy ID convention; non-matching lines are harmless.

# --- Operator RBAC (inherent to the operator's function) ---
# The Kubemoot operator manages CRD-owned workloads/pods, generates per-agent
# ConfigMaps, replicates secrets into crew namespaces (namespace-lifecycle), and
# programs the gateway. These permissions ARE the operator; removing them breaks
# reconciliation. Runtime blast radius is constrained by the pod securityContext
# (runAsNonRoot, drop ALL caps, seccomp RuntimeDefault, readonly rootfs).
KSV0041
KSV-0041
AVD-KSV-0041
KSV0048
KSV-0048
AVD-KSV-0048
KSV0049
KSV-0049
AVD-KSV-0049
KSV0056
KSV-0056
AVD-KSV-0056

# --- Trusted registry ---
# harbor-homelab.dijure.com is the cluster's own in-cluster registry and the only
# place images are pushed/pulled (in-cluster only, by design). It is trusted.
KSV0125
KSV-0125
AVD-KSV-0125

# --- Docker HEALTHCHECK not applicable in Kubernetes ---
# Liveness/readiness are declared as Kubernetes probes in the deployment manifests;
# a Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK is ignored by the kubelet, so it adds nothing here.
DS0026
DS-0026
AVD-DS-0026

# --- Image USER: runtime user is enforced by pod securityContext ---
# Every workload the operator creates (and the operator itself) runs with
# runAsNonRoot + runAsUser 65532 via the pod securityContext, which is the
# Kubernetes-native control. The image-level USER is redundant in this deployment.
DS0002
DS-0002
AVD-DS-0002
